  "prompt": "$$(2x-3)(\\frac{(x+2)}{(x+3)}) + \\frac{9}{(x+3)}$$\n\nWhich expression is equivalent to the given expression?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$\\frac{(2x^{2} + 7x - 6)}{(x+3)}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{(2x^{2} + x - 6)}{(x+3)}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{(2x^{2} - 5x + 15)}{(x+3)}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{(2x^{2} + x + 3)}{(x+3)}$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "D",
  "explanation": "First, distribute $(2x-3)$ across $\\frac{x+2}{x+3}$: $(2x-3)\\left(\\frac{x+2}{x+3}\\right) = \\frac{(2x-3)(x+2)}{x+3} = \\frac{2x^2+4x-3x-6}{x+3} = \\frac{2x^2+x-6}{x+3}$. Then add $\\frac{9}{x+3}$: $\\frac{2x^2+x-6}{x+3} + \\frac{9}{x+3} = \\frac{2x^2+x-6+9}{x+3} = \\frac{2x^2+x+3}{x+3}$.",
